# Requisicoes prontas para testar o servidor.
# Funcionam no IntelliJ IDEA (HTTP Client) e no VS Code (extensao REST Client).
# Suba a aplicacao antes (mvn spring-boot:run) e clique no "play" ao lado de cada requisicao.

@fhir = http://localhost:8080/fhir
@api = http://localhost:8080/api

### API proprietaria (ja funciona): pacientes no formato do sistema
GET {{api}}/pacientes

### API proprietaria: sinais vitais do paciente 1
GET {{api}}/sinais-vitais?pacienteId=1

### FHIR: CapabilityStatement (o que o servidor declara que sabe fazer)
GET {{fhir}}/metadata

### FHIR: ler Patient
GET {{fhir}}/Patient/1

### FHIR: Patient inexistente (esperado 404 com OperationOutcome)
GET {{fhir}}/Patient/9999

### FHIR: criar Patient (esperado 201 e cabecalho Location)
POST {{fhir}}/Patient
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

< ./exemplos/patient-valido.json

### FHIR: criar Patient invalido (esperado 4xx com OperationOutcome)
POST {{fhir}}/Patient
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

< ./exemplos/patient-invalido-sem-cpf.json

### FHIR: atualizar Patient/2 (PUT substitui o recurso inteiro; o id do corpo deve ser igual ao da URL)
PUT {{fhir}}/Patient/2
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "Patient",
  "id": "2",
  "identifier": [
    { "use": "official", "system": "http://rnds.saude.gov.br/fhir/r4/NamingSystem/cpf", "value": "08301661305" }
  ],
  "active": true,
  "name": [ { "use": "official", "family": "Oliveira Santos", "given": ["João", "Pedro"] } ],
  "telecom": [ { "system": "phone", "value": "(51) 91234-0000" } ],
  "gender": "male",
  "birthDate": "1972-11-30"
}

### FHIR: ler Observation
GET {{fhir}}/Observation/1

### FHIR: criar Observation
POST {{fhir}}/Observation
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

< ./exemplos/observation-valida.json

### FHIR: criar Observation com unidade errada (esperado 4xx)
POST {{fhir}}/Observation
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

< ./exemplos/observation-invalida-unidade.json

### FHIR: ler AllergyIntolerance
GET {{fhir}}/AllergyIntolerance/1

### FHIR: criar AllergyIntolerance
POST {{fhir}}/AllergyIntolerance
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

< ./exemplos/allergyintolerance-valida.json

### FHIR: AllergyIntolerance que viola ait-2 (esperado 4xx)
POST {{fhir}}/AllergyIntolerance
Content-Type: application/fhir+json

< ./exemplos/allergyintolerance-invalida-ait2.json
